  "articleBody": "It's totally natural to be concerned about privacy when you're thinking about adding a guest tiny home to your property. After all, you want your guests to feel comfortable and independent, and you want to maintain your own peace and quiet too! The good news is, with smart design and placement, a guest tiny home can absolutely offer both. We've helped plenty of San Diego homeowners achieve this balance.\n\nFirst, think about the orientation of the tiny home on your property. Positioning it so that its main windows or entrance don't directly face your primary home's private spaces can make a huge difference. Sometimes a little angling is all it takes! Next, consider landscaping as your best friend for privacy. Thoughtfully placed trees, shrubs, or even a nice trellis with climbing plants can create natural visual and sound barriers. Also, interior design plays a part; clever layouts can separate sleeping and living areas within the tiny home itself, giving guests their own distinct zones. Finally, discuss access points. A separate pathway or entrance can enhance the feeling of independence for your guests and reduce disturbances for you. It’s all about creating intentional boundaries.\n\nWhen you're ready to explore how a guest home can truly complement your property without sacrificing anyone's privacy, let's chat. We can help you navigate these design considerations to create a seamless experience for everyone.",
